<section class="faq-section">
  <div class="container" data-reveal-group>
    <!-- Category 1: General -->
    <div class="faq-category" data-reveal>
      <h3 class="faq-category-title">1. General</h3>
      <div class="faq-list">

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-1">
            <span>What is a disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-1">
              <p>A disposal bin is a bin that we deliver directly to your home, business, or project site. You load the bin at your own pace, and when you're finished, we pick it up and take care of the disposal.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-2">
            <span>How does the disposal bin rental process work?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-2">
              <p>Choose your preferred rental dates, submit a request, and we'll confirm availability with you. Once your rental is confirmed, we'll deliver the disposal bin to your location. You fill it at your own pace, and we'll come back to pick it up when you're done.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-3">
            <span>How far in advance should I book my disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-3">
              <p>We recommend requesting your disposal bin as early as possible, especially for weekends and busy periods. Last-minute requests may be available depending on availability.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-4">
            <span>Is my booking confirmed when I submit the online form?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-4">
              <p>No. Submitting a request does not guarantee availability or confirm your rental. A member of the Ridgeway Rentals team will review your requested dates and disposal bin availability and contact you to confirm your rental.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Category 2: Disposal Bin & Size -->
    <div class="faq-category" data-reveal>
      <h3 class="faq-category-title">2. Disposal Bin Size & Loading</h3>
      <div class="faq-list">

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-5">
            <span>What size disposal bin do you offer?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-5">
              <p>We currently offer one disposal bin size: 5 × 8.5 ft. It is suitable for household cleanouts, renovations, construction projects, landscaping, and other disposal needs.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-6">
            <span>How much weight can I put in the disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-6">
              <p>The standard rental includes up to <strong>500 kg</strong> of disposal weight. Material exceeding 500 kg is subject to an additional charge of <strong>$2 per kilogram</strong>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-7">
            <span>What happens if I exceed the included weight?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-7">
              <p>
                The standard rental includes disposal of up to <strong>500 kg</strong> of material.
                Additional weight is charged at <strong>$2 per kilogram</strong> over the included 500 kg allowance.
                The disposal facility's measured weight will be used to determine the disposal weight where applicable.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-8">
            <span>Can I fill the disposal bin above the sides?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-8">
              <p>No. All materials must remain completely inside the disposal bin. Nothing may extend above the top edge or hang over the sides, front, or rear. The load must also be reasonably level and evenly distributed.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-9">
            <span>How should I load the disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-9">
              <p>
                Materials must remain completely inside the disposal bin. The load should
                be reasonably level and evenly distributed, with no material extending above
                the top edge or hanging over the sides, front, or rear. The disposal bin
                doors must also be able to completely close and securely latch before pickup.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Category 3: What can I put in it? -->
    <div class="faq-category" data-reveal>
      <h3 class="faq-category-title">3. What Can I Put in the Disposal Bin?</h3>
      <div class="faq-list">

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-10">
            <span>What items are NOT accepted in the disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-10">
              <p>
                Certain materials are strictly prohibited, including tires, asbestos, hazardous
                materials, fuels, propane or compressed gas cylinders, paint and solvents,
                automotive fluids, pesticides, hazardous batteries, medical or biomedical waste,
                liquid waste, hot ashes or coals, burning or smouldering materials, animal
                carcasses, and other materials prohibited by the receiving disposal facility or
                applicable law.
              </p>
              <p>
                For the complete list of prohibited materials, please review our
                <a href="/terms/#prohibited-items" class="underline">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <b>Not sure if something is permitted?</b>
                <a href="/contact/" class="underline">Contact us</a> before placing it in the disposal bin.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-11">
            <span>Can I put furniture in the disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-11">
              <p>Furniture may be placed in the disposal bin as long as it does not contain prohibited materials and is loaded safely within the disposal bin's weight and loading requirements.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-12">
            <span>Can I put construction or renovation debris in the disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-12">
              <p>Construction and renovation debris can be placed in the disposal bin, provided the materials comply with our <a href="/terms/" class="underline">Terms &amp; Conditions</a> and are loaded safely. Concrete, soil, dirt, roofing shingles, and similar heavy materials require advance notification and must be loaded according to Ridgeway Rentals' instructions.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-13">
            <span>Can I put concrete, soil, dirt or other heavy materials in the disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-13">
              <p>Yes, but Ridgeway Rentals must be notified <strong>before</strong> any concrete, soil, dirt, roofing shingles, or similar heavy materials are placed in the disposal bin. These materials must be kept separate from other waste and loaded according to Ridgeway Rentals' instructions.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Category 4: Delivery -->
    <div class="faq-category" data-reveal>
      <h3 class="faq-category-title">4. Delivery</h3>
      <div class="faq-list">

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-14">
            <span>Where can you place the disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-14">
              <p>The disposal bin must be placed in a safe, firm, level, and accessible location. We will make reasonable efforts to place it where requested, but the driver has final discretion based on safety, accessibility, ground conditions, overhead clearances, and the ability to safely retrieve the loaded disposal bin.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-15">
            <span>Do I need to be home when the disposal bin is delivered?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-15">
              <p><a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" class="underline">Call</a> or <a href="/contact/" class="underline">email</a> Ridgeway Rentals to coordinate delivery arrangements. We'll work with you to confirm the delivery location and any instructions needed for access and placement.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-16">
            <span>How much space do I need for the disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-16">
              <p>Please allow approximately <strong>8 ft wide by 15 ft long</strong> for access. The delivery area must also be safe, firm, level, and accessible, with sufficient clearance for the truck to safely deliver and retrieve the disposal bin.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-17">
            <span>Can the disposal bin be delivered to a business or construction site?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-17">
              <p>Yes. We can deliver to residential, commercial, and project locations where access and placement are suitable.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Category 5: Rental Period & Pickup -->
    <div class="faq-category" data-reveal>
      <h3 class="faq-category-title">5. Rental Period & Pickup</h3>
      <div class="faq-list">

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-18">
            <span>How long can I keep the disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-18">
              <p>The standard rental period is up to 7 days from the date of delivery.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-19">
            <span>Can I keep the disposal bin longer than my original rental period?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-19">
              <p>Yes, extensions may be available at <strong>$50 per additional day</strong>, subject to disposal bin availability. <a href="/contact/" class="underline">Contact Ridgeway Rentals</a> before the end of your rental period if you need additional time. Extensions are not guaranteed.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-20">
            <span>What happens when I'm finished with the disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-20">
              <p>Once you're finished, we'll pick up the disposal bin on the scheduled pickup date. If you finish early, <a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" class="underline">call</a> or <a href="/contact/" class="underline">email</a> Ridgeway Rentals to arrange an earlier pickup.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-21">
            <span>Can I request an earlier pickup?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-21">
              <p>Yes. Early pickup is available at the same cost as the standard rental rate. <a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" class="underline">Call</a> or <a href="/contact/" class="underline">email</a> Ridgeway Rentals to arrange an earlier pickup.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-22">
            <span>What happens if the disposal bin can't be picked up?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-22">
              <p>
                The disposal bin must be safely accessible on the scheduled pickup date.
                A <strong>$50 failed pickup fee</strong> may apply if Ridgeway Rentals is unable to retrieve
                the disposal bin because of circumstances within the Renter's control,
                such as blocked access, an overloaded or improperly loaded bin, prohibited
                materials, or unsafe site conditions.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Category 6: Pricing -->
    <div class="faq-category" data-reveal>
      <h3 class="faq-category-title">6. Pricing</h3>
      <div class="faq-list">

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-23">
            <span>How much does it cost to rent a disposal bin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-23">
              <p>The standard rental fee is <strong>$395 plus applicable taxes</strong>. The standard rental period is up to 7 days and includes disposal of up to 500 kg of material.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-24">
            <span>Does the rental price include disposal?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-24">
              <p>Yes. The standard rental fee includes disposal of up to 500 kg of material. Additional weight is charged at <strong>$2 per kilogram</strong> over the included 500 kg allowance.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-25">
            <span>Are there additional fees?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-25">
              <p>Additional charges may apply in certain circumstances, including:</p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>$50 per additional rental day</strong> beyond the standard 7-day period</li>
                <li><strong>$2 per kilogram</strong> over the included 500 kg disposal allowance</li>
                <li><strong>$250</strong> for an additional dump trip during the rental period</li>
                <li>A minimum <strong>$200 prohibited-item fee</strong>, plus applicable handling or disposal costs</li>
                <li>A <strong>$50 failed pickup fee</strong> when Ridgeway Rentals is unable to safely retrieve the disposal bin due to circumstances within the Renter's control</li>
              </ul>
              <p>Applicable taxes will be added where required.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-26">
            <span>Does the rental price include delivery and pickup?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-26">
              <p>The standard rental service includes delivery and pickup. <a href="/contact/" class="underline">Contact Ridgeway Rentals</a> if you have questions about delivery to your location or special access requirements.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-27">
            <span>What if I need more than one dump during my rental?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-wrapper">
            <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-27">
              <p>You can request a replacement disposal bin if you need another dump during your rental period. Each <strong>additional</strong> dump trip is <strong>$250.</strong></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

